        "identifier": "https://www.proofatlas.ai/formalizations/sendov-conjecture/",
        "note": "The earlier Lean formalization of Sendov's conjecture for all n >= 2, by Lech Mazur, reported there as 1160 files and 92816 lines with a single main theorem. Priority for the first machine-checked proof of Sendov's conjecture belongs to that work, and this repository is the second formalization of it. \"builds-on\" rather than \"independent\": no code is shared and that development was never read, but the informal proof formalized here is a digestion of its argument, so the mathematics descends from it. What is additional here is the Phelps-Rodriguez equality classification, which that formalization does not state; as far as we are aware this is its first formalization, but that is an observation about the one earlier formalization we know of and not the result of a search. The two developments are separately checkable evidence for the same theorem; no comparison of their internal arguments has been carried out.",
